.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt FIND 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm find
.Nd traverse a directory tree and select entries
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar path ...
.Op Fl name Ar pattern
.Op Fl type Ar f|d|l
.Op Fl perm Ar mode
.Op Fl print
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility traverses each
.Ar path
(default
.Pa . )
and prints entries that match the predicates.
Symbolic links are not followed, so a link loop cannot recurse.
.Pp
The predicates are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl name Ar pattern
Match the final path component against a shell pattern with
.Ql *
and
.Ql ? .
.It Fl type Ar f|d|l
Match a regular file, directory or symbolic link.
.It Fl perm Ar mode
Match the exact octal permission bits.
.It Fl print
Print matching paths; this is the default action.
.El
.Pp
The optional
.Fl exec
action is not implemented; an unknown option is a usage error.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A missing start path or traversal error exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr file 1 ,
.Xr ls 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
